      "source": "Salem Tavern, Old Salem, NC",
      "description": "This is the Salem Tavern, located on South Main Street in the Old Salem Historic District in Winston-Salem, North Carolina.  Constructed in 1784, the building was where George Washington stayed during his Southern Tour in 1791.  It is a contributing building in the Old Salem Historic District, listed on the National Register of Historic Places and as a National Landmark Historic District in 1966.",
